# The "secret" below is NOT a secret — it is a deliberately committed, local-development-only
# credential for the Umbraco MCP server (.mcp.json), so every developer who pulls this project
# has a working MCP setup with zero configuration.
#
# Why this is safe:
#   - The MCPUSER API user is only created when ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT is Development or Local
#     (see Umbraco.Bench.Umbraco/Notifications/McpApiUserHandler.cs).
#   - On any other environment that same handler DELETES the user if it exists (protects
#     against dev databases being copied to staging/production).
#   - The value grants nothing anywhere except a developer's own local instance.
#
# Fingerprints (file:rule:line) for the committed local-only MCP credential:
.mcp.json:generic-api-key:9
Umbraco.Bench.Umbraco/Notifications/McpApiUserHandler.cs:generic-api-key:25
